  "@id": "bioconda:bioconductor-csar",
  "@type": "schema1:SoftwareApplication",
  "schema1:alternateName": "Statistical tools for the analysis of ChIP-seq data",
  "schema1:description": "Statistical tools for ChIP-seq data analysis. The package includes the statistical method described in Kaufmann et al. (2009) PLoS Biology: 7(4):e1000090. Briefly, Taking the average DNA fragment size subjected to sequencing into account, the software calculates genomic single-nucleotide read-enrichment values. After normalization, sample and control are compared using a test based on the Poisson distribution. Test statistic thresholds to control the false discovery rate are obtained through random permutation.",
  "schema1:identifier": {
    "@id": "biotools:csar"
  },
